1
00:00:00,511 --> 00:00:04,153
[SPEAKER_01]: All right, so you walk up to a couple of marines who are staying there.

2
00:00:05,934 --> 00:00:12,378
[SPEAKER_01]: I walk up and go, excuse me, officers, if I may call you that?

3
00:00:13,479 --> 00:00:13,959
[SPEAKER_01]: Officers.

4
00:00:14,379 --> 00:00:14,839
[SPEAKER_01]: What do you want?

5
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:18,341
[SPEAKER_01]: Is there any reason why you're patrolling the docks?

6
00:00:18,982 --> 00:00:24,145
[SPEAKER_01]: I feel as if your guys' presence, there must be something awry.

7
00:00:25,966 --> 00:00:26,386
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

8
00:00:29,180 --> 00:00:31,401
[SPEAKER_00]: Captain orders to have a detachment down here.

9
00:00:31,421 --> 00:00:36,363
[SPEAKER_00]: Apparently there was some bloodshed a night ago or so.

10
00:00:36,503 --> 00:00:37,323
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh my goodness, where?

11
00:00:38,123 --> 00:00:39,644
[SPEAKER_00]: In a place called the Chart Room.

12
00:00:40,684 --> 00:00:42,545
[SPEAKER_00]: Bunch of ne'er-de-wells were there.

13
00:00:42,805 --> 00:00:49,848
[SPEAKER_00]: Apparently, however, the men that killed them were a little bit more skilled than many.

14
00:00:52,028 --> 00:00:54,990
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh my goodness, are we okay?

15
00:00:55,030 --> 00:00:55,730
[SPEAKER_00]: As anyone is.

16
00:00:58,836 --> 00:01:01,416
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, thank you.

17
00:01:01,436 --> 00:01:05,797
[SPEAKER_01]: That puts me more at ease.

18
00:01:07,057 --> 00:01:09,238
[SPEAKER_01]: If I could ask you one last thing.

19
00:01:10,618 --> 00:01:12,238
[SPEAKER_01]: I have seemed to...

20
00:01:13,979 --> 00:01:26,901
[SPEAKER_01]: I lost my company of who I was working for, and I have no idea how to travel and trade

21
00:01:28,570 --> 00:01:29,911
[SPEAKER_01]: In this land.

22
00:01:30,512 --> 00:01:31,333
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, you're a merchant?

23
00:01:31,633 --> 00:01:41,502
[SPEAKER_01]: I am a merchant and I've been trying to trade back to Monmurg, of all places, to get some more goods.

24
00:01:41,562 --> 00:01:42,783
[SPEAKER_00]: Monmurg shut down.

25
00:01:43,884 --> 00:01:44,825
[SPEAKER_00]: No one goes there now.

26
00:01:45,366 --> 00:01:46,507
[SPEAKER_00]: Order the Duke of Gratzel.

27
00:01:47,520 --> 00:01:48,321
[SPEAKER_01]: Understandable.

28
00:01:48,601 --> 00:01:52,465
[SPEAKER_01]: I just, I figured I would at least try and get some stuff back here.

29
00:01:52,485 --> 00:01:57,090
[SPEAKER_00]: I've heard that there is a new dock opening up in Saltmarsh if you want to go there.

30
00:01:57,710 --> 00:01:59,452
[SPEAKER_00]: Or you can take your wares to Seton.

31
00:01:59,472 --> 00:02:01,014
[SPEAKER_00]: There are ships that go there if you'd like.

32
00:02:02,095 --> 00:02:04,257
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, I appreciate it.

33
00:02:04,317 --> 00:02:05,458
[SPEAKER_01]: It was Officer, correct?

34
00:02:06,839 --> 00:02:08,021
[SPEAKER_01]: You can call me Sergeant.

35
00:02:08,341 --> 00:02:09,002
[SPEAKER_01]: Thank you, Sergeant.

36
00:02:10,593 --> 00:02:13,236
[SPEAKER_01]: This place is a lot safer with you around.

37
00:02:13,717 --> 00:02:15,098
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, it is.

38
00:02:15,339 --> 00:02:17,942
[SPEAKER_00]: We don't want those foreign spies to cause any more trouble.

39
00:02:18,462 --> 00:02:18,803
[SPEAKER_00]: Thank you.

40
00:02:18,903 --> 00:02:21,326
[SPEAKER_01]: And I shake his hand, but it's very limp.

41
00:02:21,706 --> 00:02:22,227
[SPEAKER_01]: Like clammy.

